Summary: Let Wine's Vulkan find MoltenVK (portability enumeration)
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: gcenx
  Commit: 83ca5d2b3104
  URL: https://github.com/Gcenx/macports-wine/blob/fc0301b4896daf29bdf7140d7c67ed01f12aaacd/emulators/wine-devel/files/0001-win32u-Enable-host-Vulkan-portability-enumeration.diff
  File: emulators/wine-devel/files/0001-win32u-Enable-host-Vulkan-portability-enumeration.diff
  Changes: verbatim (context differs: 10.20 has no
    get_physical_device_properties2 line)
Upstream: pending (MR !11538; Gcenx, opened 2026-07-31, open on 2026-11-25; not
 in master at 11.22)
Needed until: MR !11538 is merged
Why: MoltenVK is a "portability" Vulkan driver: the Vulkan loader offers it
 only to an instance created with VK_KHR_portability_enumeration and
 VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR. Wine's host instance
 (win32u) asks for neither, so with the loader this project bundles
 (libvulkan.1.dylib) vkCreateInstance fails with VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER
 and Vulkan, and anything layered on it, has no device. Gcenx added this
 (macports-wine 83ca5d2b3104) when his builds moved from MoltenVK as libvulkan
 to the loader. When the host offers the extension, it's now enabled and the
 flag set.
Programs: none known; every Vulkan user (DXVK, vkd3d, wined3d's Vulkan
 renderer) would find no device
Seen on: macOS 26.7.2 (a native x86_64 program with the 11.22 build0's bundled
 loader and MoltenVK manifest: vkCreateInstance returns
 VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER without portability enumeration, and finds one
 GPU with it)
References: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11538
Related: ntdll-vulkan-bundled-driver; that one makes the loader find
 MoltenVK's manifest, this one makes it offer the driver
No test: build/smoke.sh's Vulkan step creates an instance and finds a GPU,
 which fails without this

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -448,6 +448,11 @@
 
     if (instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_win32_surface && vulkan_funcs.host_extensions.has_VK_EXT_surface_maintenance1)
         instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_EXT_surface_maintenance1 = 1;
+    if (vulkan_funcs.host_extensions.has_VK_KHR_portability_enumeration)
+    {
+        instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_portability_enumeration = 1;
+        info->flags |= VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR;
+    }
     if (use_external_memory())
     {
         instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_get_physical_device_properties2 = 1;
